#: src/bare-metal/aps/safemmio/registers.md:6
msgid "safe-mmio"
msgstr ""

#: src/bare-metal/aps/safemmio/registers.md:8
msgid ""
"The [`safe-mmio`](https://crates.io/crates/safe-mmio) crate provides types "
"to wrap registers that can be read or written safely."
msgstr ""

#: src/bare-metal/aps/safemmio/registers.md:11
msgid "Can't read"
msgstr ""

#: src/bare-metal/aps/safemmio/registers.md:11
msgid "Read has no side-effects"
msgstr ""

#: src/bare-metal/aps/safemmio/registers.md:11
msgid "Read has side-effects"
msgstr ""

#: src/bare-metal/aps/safemmio/registers.md:13
msgid "Can't write"
msgstr ""

#: src/bare-metal/aps/safemmio/registers.md:13
msgid ""
"[`ReadPure`](https://docs.rs/safe-mmio/latest/safe_mmio/fields/struct."
"ReadPure.html)"
msgstr ""

#: src/bare-metal/aps/safemmio/registers.md:13
msgid ""
"[`ReadOnly`](https://docs.rs/safe-mmio/latest/safe_mmio/fields/struct."
"ReadOnly.html)"
msgstr ""

#: src/bare-metal/aps/safemmio/registers.md:14
msgid "Can write"
msgstr ""

#: src/bare-metal/aps/safemmio/registers.md:14
msgid ""
"[`WriteOnly`](https://docs.rs/safe-mmio/latest/safe_mmio/fields/struct."
"WriteOnly.html)"
msgstr ""

#: src/bare-metal/aps/safemmio/registers.md:14
msgid ""
"[`ReadPureWrite`](https://docs.rs/safe-mmio/latest/safe_mmio/fields/struct."
"ReadPureWrite.html)"
msgstr ""

#: src/bare-metal/aps/safemmio/registers.md:14
msgid ""
"[`ReadWrite`](https://docs.rs/safe-mmio/latest/safe_mmio/fields/struct."
"ReadWrite.html)"
msgstr ""

#: src/bare-metal/aps/safemmio/registers.md:57
msgid "Reading `dr` has a side effect: it pops a byte from the receive FIFO."
msgstr ""

#: src/bare-metal/aps/safemmio/registers.md:58
msgid ""
"Reading `rsr` (and other registers) has no side-effects. It is a 'pure' read."
msgstr ""

#: src/bare-metal/aps/safemmio/registers.md:62
msgid ""
"There are a number of different crates providing safe abstractions around "
"MMIO operations; we recommend the `safe-mmio` crate."
msgstr ""

#: src/bare-metal/aps/safemmio/registers.md:64
msgid ""
"The difference between `ReadPure` or `ReadOnly` (and likewise between "
"`ReadPureWrite` and `ReadWrite`) is whether reading a register can have side-"
"effects that change the state of the device, e.g., reading the data register "
"pops a byte from the receive FIFO. `ReadPure` means that reads have no side-"
"effects, they are purely reading data."
msgstr ""
